{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Shadow",
  "author": "Unknown",
  "pages": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Shadow",
        "(A calm bedtime retelling)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "paragraphs": [
        "In a warm city where the streets glowed at sunset, there lived a learned man.",
        "He liked books.",
        "He liked ideas.",
        "He liked quiet evenings when the air felt soft and still."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "paragraphs": [
        "One night, he sat on a balcony.",
        "Across the courtyard was a bright house.",
        "Music drifted from its windows.",
        "Light spilled onto the walls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The learned man watched.",
        "And beside him, his shadow stretched long on the ground."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "paragraphs": [
        "“Look,” the learned man said softly, as if speaking to himself.",
        "“It seems so lively over there.",
        "I wonder what is happening.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "paragraphs": [
        "And as the light shifted…",
        "Something strange happened."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The shadow moved.",
        "Not just the way shadows move.",
        "But as if it were deciding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p8",
      "paragraphs": [
        "It slipped away from the learned man.",
        "Crossed the courtyard.",
        "And disappeared into the bright house."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p9",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The learned man blinked.",
        "He rubbed his eyes.",
        "But the shadow did not return."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p10",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Days passed.",
        "The learned man felt oddly lighter.",
        "And oddly lonelier.",
        "As if a quiet companion had gone away."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p11",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Years passed.",
        "And one day, a visitor arrived.",
        "A tall gentleman.",
        "Well dressed.",
        "Confident."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p12",
      "paragraphs": [
        "He bowed.",
        "“Do you remember me?” the visitor asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p13",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The learned man stared.",
        "“I… do not,” he said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p14",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The visitor smiled.",
        "“I am your shadow,” he said.",
        "“I went out into the world.",
        "I learned many things.",
        "And now I have returned.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p15",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The learned man felt a chill.",
        "Because the visitor did not feel like a shadow anymore.",
        "He felt like someone in charge."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p16",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The shadow spoke smoothly.",
        "He told stories.",
        "He made jokes.",
        "He knew how to charm a room."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p17",
      "paragraphs": [
        "People listened.",
        "People admired him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p18",
      "paragraphs": [
        "And the learned man—quiet and thoughtful—was ignored."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p19",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The shadow began to say,",
        "“Come with me.",
        "Let me lead.",
        "You can follow.",
        "It will be easier that way.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p20",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The learned man felt uneasy.",
        "Because a shadow is meant to follow.",
        "Not to command."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p21",
      "paragraphs": [
        "But the world can be dazzled by confidence.",
        "Even when confidence is empty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p22",
      "paragraphs": [
        "So the learned man made a choice.",
        "He stepped back.",
        "He became careful.",
        "He protected what was true inside him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p23",
      "paragraphs": [
        "And in the quiet of his own room, he remembered something important:",
        "That the brightest voice is not always the wisest.",
        "That the boldest presence is not always the kindest.",
        "And that we must not let anything—",
        "not pride,",
        "not fear,",
        "not a shadow—",
        "take the place of our true selves."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p24",
      "paragraphs": [
        "So he lived gently.",
        "And he held onto what mattered.",
        "Even when the world was noisy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p25",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The End!"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
